<Layout title="Privacy Policy | broker pal" description="How broker pal collects, uses, and protects information submitted through its website and loan inquiry forms.">
  <article class="privacy">
    <div class="kicker">YOUR INFORMATION</div>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective date: November 9, 2026</p>
    <p>broker pal, LLC ("broker pal," "we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This policy explains how we collect, use, and disclose information when you visit our website or submit an inquiry about investment-property financing.</p>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect contact details such as your name, email address, and telephone number; business or entity information; property address and characteristics; and financing details you choose to provide, such as estimated value, purchase price, requested loan amount, and rental income. Our website host and security tools may also process technical information such as IP address, browser details, and security events.</p>
    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use information to respond to inquiries, discuss financing options, evaluate whether a potential loan request may fit available lending programs, communicate with you, operate and secure our website, prevent fraud, and meet legal or regulatory obligations.</p>
    <h2>When information may be shared</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information. We may share information with lending partners, lenders, or other parties involved in arranging or evaluating a loan when you ask us to assist with a financing request. We may also use service providers that help operate our website, communications, security, or business systems, and disclose information when required by law or to protect rights and safety.</p>
    <h2>Communications</h2>
    <p>If you provide contact information, we may contact you about your inquiry. Marketing text messages or automated calls will not be sent unless the required consent has been obtained. You may ask us to stop non-essential communications at any time.</p>
    <h2>Security and retention</h2>
    <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures appropriate to the information and systems involved. No website or electronic transmission can be guaranteed completely secure. We retain information for as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described above, including applicable business, legal, and recordkeeping requirements.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
    <p>You may contact us to request access to, correction of, or deletion of information you provided, subject to legal and business recordkeeping obligations. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p>
    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>This website and our financing inquiry services are intended for adults and are not directed to children under 13.</p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The effective date above will reflect the most recent version.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or privacy requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:brian@yourbrokerpal.com">brian@yourbrokerpal.com</a> or by calling <a href="tel:4046062943">404-606-2943</a>.</p>
    <p class="notice"><strong>Important:</strong> The public loan inquiry form is for preliminary contact and property information only. Do not submit Social Security numbers, dates of birth, bank account information, tax returns, bank statements, or other sensitive financial documents through the public website form.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
